#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""tools/check - the local code checker: the gate every brick of docs/BUILD_PLAN.md passes.
Original code for this project. A Linux gate: on macOS only --only 5 (cleanroom) is meaningful, because the other
stages expect gcc, Linux libraries and LeakSanitizer.

usage: tools/check [--quick] [--baseline] [--new-sound] [--serial] [--only N[,N...]]
  --quick     stages 1-4 only
  --baseline  take the reference data (golden dumps, pictures, sound, frame time) from this build;
              brick 0 only, with the old libraries in place
  --new-sound   after the main theme's score or the synth was changed on purpose: stage 8 takes its reference
              render again, but only if the render passes the ear check
  --serial    one stage after another (normally stages 2-8 and 10 run side by side after the build,
              and the timing stage 9 runs alone at the end)
  --only      run just these stages (for working on one; a gate run is the full check)

Prints PASS or FAIL for every stage and exits 1 if any stage failed. The whole report is saved to
build/check/<date>-<commit>.txt (with -dirty when the tree has uncommitted changes).

The stages:
   1 build       release and ASan+UBSan, with GCC and with Clang, -Wall -Wextra -Werror on our code
   2 tests       the unit tests (ctest) in the GCC release and the Clang ASan builds
   3 golden      every JSON the game reads, dumped by our own reader and compared byte for byte with the
                 reference dumps (taken with the old reader in brick 0); every game mesh, and the same mesh
                 written to and read back from our own .glb, against its reference dump; the opening film
                 keeps every shot's subjects in frame (assets/intro/tools/frame_check.js --strict); the figure
                 engine makes the same triangles in C and in the browser game (assets/figure/parity.js)
   4 deps        what the binaries link and load, what CMake fetches, what the sources include
   5 cleanroom   no third-party names past the allow-list, no licence headers, no personal or machine
                 terms, the homage line the only reference to the original game
   6 headless    the 900-frame intro and 3,000 frames of each game mode under ASan: no crash, no leak
   7 picture     menu, cockpit and title card against their references, on the GPU (the game's own renderer,
                 headless) and with the software renderer: under 0.5 % of pixels differ
   8 sound       the main theme played live by the synth through the player, round its loop, against this
                 machine's reference render (2 LSB), and the ear check on it: OK or NOTE, no clicks, no
                 sudden jumps, true peak at most -1 dBTP, -20 LUFS within 1 LU
   9 perf        frame time of a fixed flight scene, software and GPU, at most 5 % above the baseline; a GPU
                 table of every map at every time of day (logged)
  10 windows     MinGW cross-build of TailonLock.exe and its import table: system DLLs only
  11 floppy      the floppy build's size: the stripped game plus the files it loads at run time (not the
                 recorded music, which is an extra), and the browser game without its recorded music, each
                 packed and xz-compressed, against 1.44 MB (a report until the F track is done, then a fail)
"""
